1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:05,088
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,386 --> 00:00:13,596
[man] <i>Congressman, a group of bandits</i>
<i>robbed the gambling den.</i>

3
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,640
<i>We lost about 100,000 pesos.</i>

4
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:18,977
[Julio] <i>I'm putting up</i>
<i>a 100,000-peso reward</i>

5
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:23,064
<i>for every bandit they catch.</i>

6
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:25,024
<i>Dead or alive.</i>

7
00:00:25,108 --> 00:00:28,111
[Fernan] <i>We have the same goal,</i>
<i>but different perspectives.</i>

8
00:00:28,194 --> 00:00:31,114
<i>I just hope we can work together</i>
<i>to fight against the Ardientes.</i>

9
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:33,199
[reporter] <i>Is there any truth</i>
<i>to the allegations against you?</i>

10
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:34,451
<i>You shameless thieves!</i>

11
00:00:34,534 --> 00:00:36,494
[Emilia screaming] <i>Hey! Ouch!</i>

12
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:40,457
<i>Whoever's spreading rumors</i>
<i>about our family, come out!</i>

13
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:44,002
[Ivy] <i>This is only the beginning</i>
<i>of our battle against the Ardientes.</i>

14
00:00:44,085 --> 00:00:45,420
<i>And I promise you,</i>

15
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:48,089
<i>the Ardientes are going down, Mom.</i>

16
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:50,008
<i>She's not the only one behind this.</i>

17
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:52,051
<i>Someone big is backing her up.</i>

18
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:52,927
[Claire] <i>Who could that be?</i>

19
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:54,971
[Emilia] <i>Could it be her darned daughter?</i>

20
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:58,475
<i>Do you know whom I'm suspecting?</i>
<i>Miss Aguas.</i>

21
00:00:58,558 --> 00:01:00,810
<i>You don't deserve to be</i>
<i>called "Congressman".</i>

22
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:03,646
<i>You are a dirty politician,</i>
<i>and I will bring you down.</i>

23
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:05,315
<i>You can't buy me.</i>

24
00:01:05,398 --> 00:01:07,400
[Julio] <i>Julio Ardiente's wrath…</i>

25
00:01:07,484 --> 00:01:08,777
<i>-is like a hurricane.</i>
<i>-No!</i>

26
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:11,112
<i>It will destroy everything in its path.</i>

27
00:01:11,196 --> 00:01:12,197
[Ivy] <i>Suicide?!</i>

28
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,990
<i>Who does that congressman</i>
<i>think he's fooling?!</i>

29
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:16,284
<i>I'm sure he had her killed!</i>

30
00:01:16,367 --> 00:01:18,995
[Diego] <i>I'm sure Ivy's case will</i>
<i>be compromised because of this.</i>

31
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,288
<i>I need to help her.</i>

32
00:01:20,371 --> 00:01:22,999
<i>Where's Camia Cruz?</i>
<i>We want to hear her story.</i>

33
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:24,459
<i>Is someone protecting her?</i>

34
00:01:24,542 --> 00:01:25,752
<i>We need a statement on this, Attorney.</i>

35
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:27,003
<i>What is she afraid of?</i>

36
00:01:27,086 --> 00:01:29,339
<i>Ivy, you can trust me. I'll help you.</i>

37
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:31,299
<i>Even if I have to testify</i>
<i>against the family</i>

38
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:32,842
<i>who raised me, I'll do it.</i>

39
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:33,676
<i>He's right, Ivy.</i>

40
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,386
<i>We need all the help that we can get now.</i>

41
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:36,679
<i>I spoke to the judge earlier,</i>

42
00:01:36,763 --> 00:01:39,599
<i>and he's inclined to dismiss the case</i>
<i>if Camia won't show up in court.</i>

43
00:01:39,682 --> 00:01:41,434
<i>It's time for me to face them--</i>

44
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:44,437
<i>If you're going to face them, I will too.</i>

45
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:47,398
[Julio] <i>We are celebrating my victory.</i>

46
00:01:47,482 --> 00:01:50,235
<i>This case will be dismissed</i>

47
00:01:50,318 --> 00:01:52,779
<i>without Camia Cruz in the picture.</i>

48
00:01:52,862 --> 00:01:55,323
<i>We're having a grand press conference</i>
<i>for Papa tomorrow.</i>

49
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:56,699
<i>So, I want you to come with me.</i>

50
00:01:56,783 --> 00:02:00,161
<i>Mom. I know where you're going</i>
<i>to make your big reveal.</i>

51
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:04,207
<i>-I like that smile, Emilia.</i>
<i>-Smile of success, Aunt Claire.</i>

52
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:07,585
[Emilia] <i>That press conference</i>
<i>will bury him into the ground.</i>

53
00:02:07,669 --> 00:02:09,671
<i>He's in for a big surprise.</i>

54
00:02:14,926 --> 00:02:17,137
[instrumental theme music playing]

55
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:20,140
Back then,

56
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:22,517
I used to dress you up…

57
00:02:23,726 --> 00:02:26,729
and get you ready
for important events like this.

58
00:02:28,022 --> 00:02:30,483
Honestly, Mom, I still feel nervous.

59
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:33,653
Don't be, Lily.

60
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:36,656
You're much stronger
than you think you are.

61
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:39,951
In the 13 years that we were separated,

62
00:02:40,034 --> 00:02:42,912
you proved that you are a strong woman.

63
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:45,582
That you're ready for this battle.

64
00:02:51,129 --> 00:02:52,130
Come here.

65
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:56,676
I'm proud of you, Lily.

66
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:58,970
Your father and I.

67
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:01,055
So don't worry.

68
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:02,849
I know…

69
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:05,852
justice is on our side.

70
00:03:14,027 --> 00:03:18,573
I can't wait to reveal myself
to the Ardientes.

71
00:03:21,284 --> 00:03:24,078
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]
<i>♪ Let her cry ♪</i>

72
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:28,124
<i>♪ For she's a lady ♪</i>

73
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:32,879
<i>♪ Let her dream… ♪</i>

74
00:03:32,962 --> 00:03:37,508
[Filipino folk song playing]

75
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:54,067
[Filipino folk song continues playing]

76
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:15,630
[Filipino folk song continues playing]

77
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:36,109
[suspenseful music playing]

78
00:05:11,394 --> 00:05:12,979
-Ivy!
-Emilia!

79
00:05:13,062 --> 00:05:13,980
Hi!

80
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:16,441
Papa.

81
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:18,234
-Yes?
-Look who's here!

82
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:25,408
Good evening, Miss Aguas.

83
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:27,702
Long time, no see!

84
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:30,997
Indeed, Congressman. Long time, no see!

85
00:05:31,539 --> 00:05:32,957
I missed you!

86
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:37,378
That's why I accepted Emilia's invitation.

87
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:40,339
I didn't want to miss this event.

88
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:42,717
Really, now?

89
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:45,803
You know, I was under the impression…

90
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:48,473
you were hiding from me

91
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:49,891
because you did something wrong.

92
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:52,685
I did something wrong?

93
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:54,645
Tell me.

94
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:58,107
I don't think this is the venue for that.

95
00:05:58,399 --> 00:06:02,653
Congressman, you don't need a
proper venue to tell the truth.

96
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:07,617
Is it because I'm one of your suspects

97
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:10,661
behind the attacks against you?

98
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:11,746
[laughs]

99
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:15,708
Congressman, I'm not a fool to do that.

100
00:06:16,292 --> 00:06:20,296
Because I invested a lot in your family.

101
00:06:20,963 --> 00:06:23,841
And to be honest, I went away because

102
00:06:23,925 --> 00:06:26,594
I didn't want to be involved
in your family's issues.

103
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:30,056
But now that you're going
to clear your name,

104
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:32,683
I guess there won't be any more problems.

105
00:06:34,477 --> 00:06:35,978
So, shall we go in?

106
00:06:36,479 --> 00:06:38,523
-Yes.
-Papa, we'll go in. Let's go.

107
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:42,110
[tense music playing]

108
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:52,745
[Filipino folk song playing]

109
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:14,392
[applause]

110
00:07:14,475 --> 00:07:16,310
Good evening to everyone!

111
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:21,315
[host] Friends, let's all
welcome the Ardiente family!

112
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:25,278
-[applause]
-[entrance music playing]

113
00:07:35,788 --> 00:07:39,250
[applause]

114
00:07:50,803 --> 00:07:53,806
-[applause]
-[entrance music continues]

115
00:08:12,366 --> 00:08:13,993
[host] Let's give our beloved congressman

116
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:16,579
a warm round of applause.

117
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:19,707
Congressman Julio Ardiente!

118
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:22,668
[applause]

119
00:08:25,713 --> 00:08:26,714
Thank you.

120
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:31,886
Thank you. Thank you very much.
Please take your seats.

121
00:08:31,969 --> 00:08:33,137
Sit down, please.

122
00:08:35,389 --> 00:08:37,141
Good evening, ladies and gentlemen.

123
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:40,311
To my children of the fourth district.

124
00:08:41,395 --> 00:08:46,025
Thank you for coming
to this press event tonight…

125
00:08:46,817 --> 00:08:50,696
which we deliberately organized…

126
00:08:51,322 --> 00:08:56,369
to clarify all the accusations
against me and my family.

127
00:08:59,163 --> 00:09:02,708
First of all, I would like to address…

128
00:09:03,376 --> 00:09:05,753
the controversy about a woman…

129
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:10,049
named Camia Cruz.

130
00:09:10,132 --> 00:09:11,968
[tense music playing]

131
00:09:12,051 --> 00:09:14,178
-Papa.
-Yes, Emilia?

132
00:09:14,845 --> 00:09:16,222
Can I speak about her?

133
00:09:18,766 --> 00:09:19,892
By all means, go ahead.

134
00:09:28,442 --> 00:09:30,695
Camia Cruz is furious at me,

135
00:09:30,778 --> 00:09:33,614
so I should be the one
to clarify this issue.

136
00:09:35,658 --> 00:09:38,494
Camia Cruz is nothing
but a desperate woman.

137
00:09:39,078 --> 00:09:41,622
She once seduced my husband, Raul.

138
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:46,586
And as a woman, I fought for my marriage.

139
00:09:47,503 --> 00:09:51,090
But now, she's back to get what is mine.

140
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:54,051
And she's spinning all these
lies against my family…

141
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:56,679
to destroy me.

142
00:09:57,597 --> 00:10:00,683
You know, Camia Cruz,
if you're telling the truth…

143
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:02,435
then where are you?

144
00:10:05,438 --> 00:10:06,856
Why are you hiding?

145
00:10:07,356 --> 00:10:09,650
Come out! Show yourself!

146
00:10:12,194 --> 00:10:15,865
[suspenseful music playing]

147
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:28,461
[tense music playing]

148
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:44,018
Are you looking for me, Emilia?

149
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:22,515
Hello, Emilia.

150
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:24,975
Did you miss me?

151
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:32,817
And to the rest of the Ardiente family,
did you miss me too?

152
00:11:33,818 --> 00:11:36,362
Yes! I am Camia!

153
00:11:37,822 --> 00:11:40,324
And to everyone here… Can you hear me?!

154
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:42,201
I am Camia Cruz!

155
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:05,724
Well, Emilia?

156
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,562
Cat got your tongue?

157
00:12:10,938 --> 00:12:12,523
Do you want me to pull it out for you?

158
00:12:14,191 --> 00:12:15,651
Or would you prefer this?

159
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:30,791
Well, Emilia…

160
00:12:32,042 --> 00:12:33,878
[chuckles]

161
00:12:33,961 --> 00:12:35,754
Are you stressed?

162
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:43,804
I'm not a desperate woman!

163
00:12:44,847 --> 00:12:47,558
I never stole anyone's husband!

164
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:49,977
The truth is,

165
00:12:50,644 --> 00:12:53,397
you had my whole family killed!

166
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:15,085
How dare you!

167
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:17,630
-Let go of me!
-That's enough.

168
00:13:21,509 --> 00:13:23,260
Jasmin? Camia?

169
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:27,681
You're alive?

170
00:13:33,229 --> 00:13:34,563
Guards! Guards!

171
00:13:35,064 --> 00:13:36,774
[Emilia] Get her out of here!

172
00:13:36,857 --> 00:13:38,859
-She's not even invited!
-Wait.

173
00:13:38,943 --> 00:13:41,862
Who's desperate now, Emilia?

174
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:46,825
Are you scared that I'll expose
all your secrets?

175
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:52,498
Wait! Wait! Drop your guns!
Drop them! Put them down!

176
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:01,674
You dared me to show up.
So, that's what I did.

177
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:06,971
Now that I'm here, your tails
are between your legs!

178
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:13,269
These murderers tried to silence me once.

179
00:14:16,939 --> 00:14:18,065
But that won't happen again.

180
00:14:19,066 --> 00:14:23,529
Because I will reveal the truth.

181
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:25,531
Is it true they killed
your husband and daughter?

182
00:14:25,614 --> 00:14:27,575
What was their motive
for murdering your family?

183
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:28,909
Why did you only show up now?

184
00:14:37,626 --> 00:14:38,669
Ma'am, please.

185
00:14:38,836 --> 00:14:41,255
We need your testimony
against the Ardientes.

186
00:14:41,547 --> 00:14:43,424
Don't come back here again, boy.

187
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:46,677
I don't want the Ardientes
knocking on my door too.

188
00:14:46,969 --> 00:14:48,721
But they killed your husband!

189
00:14:49,138 --> 00:14:50,723
Don't you want to avenge his death?

190
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:52,558
You don't understand, boy.

191
00:14:53,017 --> 00:14:56,520
Here, the Ardientes are the law!

192
00:14:56,896 --> 00:15:00,274
And anyone who opposes them
will end up six feet under.

193
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:02,610
Especially that Camia Cruz!

194
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:05,404
So, please, just leave me alone!

195
00:15:05,487 --> 00:15:07,364
Ma'am, please I'm begging you.

196
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:09,950
Please help us help you.

197
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:11,619
I don't need your help!

198
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:15,164
Go away! Get out!

199
00:15:17,291 --> 00:15:19,335
[Camia] My husband Dante was a lawyer.

200
00:15:19,418 --> 00:15:21,003
We moved here to Poblacion Ardiente

201
00:15:21,086 --> 00:15:22,546
because he was assigned here.

202
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:25,341
While working for the attorney's office,

203
00:15:25,424 --> 00:15:29,553
Dante discovered all the
Ardientes' dirty secrets!

204
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:34,058
This province never had a zero crime rate!

205
00:15:34,516 --> 00:15:37,061
Everywhere, there are people
being silenced or killed!

206
00:15:39,104 --> 00:15:42,316
And the Ardientes are the ones behind it!

207
00:15:42,983 --> 00:15:44,568
The attorney's office

208
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:46,445
was a front for them
to conceal their crimes!

209
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:48,739
[thumps cane]

210
00:15:49,406 --> 00:15:55,204
[thumps cane]

211
00:15:56,288 --> 00:15:57,456
Bravo!

212
00:15:58,707 --> 00:15:59,833
[Julio] Wonderful!

213
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:03,921
Such a well-written speech!

214
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:07,758
You delivered it well too.

215
00:16:08,717 --> 00:16:12,096
But this will all remain
to be a narrative.

216
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:17,017
There's no truth behind
this woman's allegations.

217
00:16:18,435 --> 00:16:21,480
You're grasping at straws
that aren't there.

218
00:16:21,563 --> 00:16:23,732
I can prove everything I've said.

219
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:24,942
[Julio] Prove what?!

220
00:16:25,484 --> 00:16:30,406
That my political rivals paid
your husband to ruin my image?

221
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:33,075
Dante Cruz was an honest public servant!

222
00:16:33,158 --> 00:16:34,451
Oh, shut up!

223
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:37,663
Are you sure about that?

224
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:41,041
[Emilia] Your husband went to
my office a couple of times.

225
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:44,336
He would fabricating
allegations against me…

226
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:46,130
so he could extort money from me.

227
00:16:46,839 --> 00:16:49,633
You know, it hurts to admit this,

228
00:16:49,717 --> 00:16:51,427
but I want everyone to know that…

229
00:16:52,219 --> 00:16:54,471
you ruined my marriage!

230
00:16:55,347 --> 00:16:57,391
That woman ruined my marriage!

231
00:16:58,183 --> 00:16:59,810
Weren't you Diego's tutor?

232
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:02,604
But instead of teaching my son,

233
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:05,065
you stole my husband!

234
00:17:15,868 --> 00:17:19,580
[phone ringing]

235
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:23,917
-Hello, Nanny?
-Hello, Diego?

236
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:27,588
Lily's mother, Miss Camia…

237
00:17:27,671 --> 00:17:28,839
finally showed herself.

238
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:32,718
She's on TV. She's confronting
your mother and grandfather.

239
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:34,136
<i>It's scary!</i>

240
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:36,680
Why? What did they do to her?!

241
00:17:37,389 --> 00:17:38,891
<i>They humiliated her.</i>

242
00:17:39,683 --> 00:17:41,602
Your mother called her a mistress.

243
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:45,814
<i>They're saying that she agreed</i>
<i>to be your tutor then…</i>

244
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:47,858
because she wanted to seduce Raul.

245
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:49,276
They're all liars!

246
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:51,653
I'll go to the press conference.

247
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:53,030
I'll get to the bottom of this.

248
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:55,657
-Be careful, Diego.
-I will.

249
00:17:59,453 --> 00:18:02,039
I stole your husband?!

250
00:18:03,248 --> 00:18:07,002
Why don't we let Raul
tell us what really happened?!

251
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:09,755
Is your wife
telling the truth, Mr. Torillo?

252
00:18:11,423 --> 00:18:14,635
No! He is not going
to give any statements now!

253
00:18:14,718 --> 00:18:16,637
[scoffs] See that?

254
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:19,389
You're such a liar, Emilia!

255
00:18:20,974 --> 00:18:22,017
The truth is…

256
00:18:23,268 --> 00:18:26,522
your husband attempted to rape me!

257
00:18:28,023 --> 00:18:31,652
Dante wanted to bring him to
justice, so you had him killed!

258
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:32,861
You poisoned him!

259
00:18:35,322 --> 00:18:36,657
But that's not all!

260
00:18:37,991 --> 00:18:40,202
You ordered to have me
and my daughter killed!

261
00:18:43,664 --> 00:18:45,541
But the time has come…

262
00:18:48,001 --> 00:18:50,587
for justice to be served.

263
00:18:51,755 --> 00:18:55,300
It's time for you to pay
for what you've done

264
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:59,012
to the people of Poblacion Ardiente!

265
00:19:02,349 --> 00:19:03,684
I swear…

266
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:06,311
After this…

267
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:10,315
no Ardiente will ever hurt

268
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:12,693
or abuse anyone again!

269
00:19:25,372 --> 00:19:27,583
[Julio] Well, well, well…

270
00:19:30,544 --> 00:19:31,670
It looks like…

271
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:35,966
this press conference
has turned into a witch-hunt!

272
00:19:37,509 --> 00:19:39,469
It's her word against ours.

273
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:46,393
It's best for us to end
this party early tonight.

274
00:19:47,311 --> 00:19:50,731
This will only lead to gossiping…

275
00:19:52,274 --> 00:20:00,115
while nothing this woman
has said is proven.

276
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:03,994
Everything that comes out of her mouth…

277
00:20:04,995 --> 00:20:07,122
can't really be trusted.

278
00:20:09,291 --> 00:20:14,880
[tense music swelling]

279
00:20:19,343 --> 00:20:21,345
I'll see you in court…

280
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:24,640
Camia Cruz.

281
00:20:25,057 --> 00:20:28,477
To all of you, thank you for accepting

282
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:31,021
the invitation of the Ardientes.

283
00:20:32,439 --> 00:20:33,565
[Emilia] Raul, let's go.

284
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:50,332
Raul!

285
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:52,292
Let's go!

286
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:06,390
[tense music continues playing]

287
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:24,658
-Congressman!
-Congressman.

288
00:21:24,741 --> 00:21:25,951
Congressman!

289
00:21:26,034 --> 00:21:29,579
Is it true that ex-governor
Emilia Ardiente-Torillo

290
00:21:29,663 --> 00:21:31,248
had Camia Cruz's family killed?

291
00:21:32,416 --> 00:21:36,586
Everything Miss Camia Cruz says is a lie.

292
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:39,840
They're all fabricated lies to destroy me…

293
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:44,094
to destroy my name, to destroy our family.

294
00:21:45,345 --> 00:21:48,473
Come now, you know us.
You know the Ardientes.

295
00:21:48,849 --> 00:21:53,020
For so many years, we have
served the public faithfully.

296
00:21:53,437 --> 00:21:55,272
You've followed our career.

297
00:21:55,355 --> 00:21:59,109
You know that we have
an excellent track record

298
00:21:59,192 --> 00:22:01,528
when it comes to public service.

299
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:04,156
Based on that,

300
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:07,576
you'll see that we're honest and sincere.

301
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:10,787
That's why I'm not worried or afraid

302
00:22:10,871 --> 00:22:12,789
of Miss Cruz's threats.

303
00:22:13,248 --> 00:22:14,750
I know that in court,

304
00:22:14,833 --> 00:22:18,295
all her charges against
us will be proven false.

305
00:22:19,254 --> 00:22:20,505
The Ardiente family…

306
00:22:21,381 --> 00:22:23,717
will continue to serve the people.

307
00:22:24,217 --> 00:22:25,218
Viva Ardiente!

308
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:26,511
-Viva Ardiente!
-Viva Ardiente!

309
00:22:26,928 --> 00:22:28,555
Now, if you'll excuse us…

310
00:22:28,638 --> 00:22:29,723
Thank you, Congressman.

311
00:22:29,806 --> 00:22:31,725
-Thank you too.
-What do you plan on doing next?

312
00:22:31,808 --> 00:22:35,145
[Julio] Well, it all depends on Miss Camia

313
00:22:35,228 --> 00:22:38,106
and how she plans
on disturbing our family.

314
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:40,692
Then, we will just reciprocate.

315
00:22:47,532 --> 00:22:49,451
[reporter] So, what will be
your next move, Miss Cruz?

316
00:22:49,534 --> 00:22:51,036
The Ardientes are very influential people.

317
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:53,205
How will this affect
your position in court?

318
00:22:53,288 --> 00:22:55,540
The Ardientes might be influential,

319
00:22:55,624 --> 00:22:57,459
but I'm not backing down from the case.

320
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:00,295
[Camia] I believe that

321
00:23:00,378 --> 00:23:04,341
the truth will prevail
against their power.

322
00:23:04,424 --> 00:23:06,927
You mentioned your husband
and daughter were murdered.

323
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:09,304
Isn't it hard to fight this battle alone?

324
00:23:13,558 --> 00:23:15,060
My daughter is always with me.

325
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:18,605
She's in my heart.

326
00:23:24,236 --> 00:23:27,322
Thank you for listening
to my story. Excuse me.

327
00:23:42,921 --> 00:23:44,548
Wait, Auntie. Where's Raul?

328
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:47,050
I don't know. He was with us just before.

329
00:23:48,135 --> 00:23:49,511
Could he be…

330
00:23:49,594 --> 00:23:51,388
Okay, I know where he is.

331
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:54,850
Emilia, wait. Madrigal, go with her.

332
00:23:57,018 --> 00:23:57,978
[exhales sharply]

333
00:24:01,481 --> 00:24:02,482
[Raul clears throat]

334
00:24:04,401 --> 00:24:06,611
Camia, can I-- Wait.

335
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,947
I just want to--
Camia, I wanna talk to you.

336
00:24:09,030 --> 00:24:10,907
-Let go of me!
-It's okay. Let him go.

337
00:24:14,119 --> 00:24:15,871
What do you want, Raul?

338
00:24:15,954 --> 00:24:17,789
Why did you come here, Camia?

339
00:24:18,456 --> 00:24:21,501
You know what they'll do to you.
They'll have you killed.

340
00:24:22,210 --> 00:24:25,213
Raul, I won't hide like a coward.

341
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:28,049
You'll all pay for this!

342
00:24:28,633 --> 00:24:30,635
[Camia] You kept me locked up
for so long, Raul.

343
00:24:31,178 --> 00:24:33,305
You imprisoned me! And for what?

344
00:24:33,847 --> 00:24:37,475
So you wouldn't have to face
the sins you've committed?!

345
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:41,021
[quietly] Lily… stay here.

346
00:24:41,897 --> 00:24:44,524
[Raul] They left you to die, Camia.

347
00:24:44,608 --> 00:24:48,570
But I didn't. I saved you.
I saved your life, Camia.

348
00:24:48,653 --> 00:24:49,404
Raul!

349
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:54,743
[Camia] Locking me up all those
years wasn't "saving" me.

350
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:58,246
You're no different from the Ardientes!

351
00:24:58,330 --> 00:25:03,251
You're the root of all
my family's misfortunes!

352
00:25:04,044 --> 00:25:06,254
You robbed me of my life!

353
00:25:08,381 --> 00:25:11,551
What can I do to earn
your forgiveness, Camia?

354
00:25:11,635 --> 00:25:14,512
I will never forgive you, Raul!

355
00:25:14,721 --> 00:25:16,806
Hey, you skank! Well?

356
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:18,725
-Well?!
-Emilia, stop it.

357
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:19,851
-Raul…
-Stop it!

358
00:25:19,935 --> 00:25:20,977
What? Why are you stopping me?

359
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:23,230
-Leave us alone.
-You're taking her side?!

360
00:25:23,688 --> 00:25:26,024
You bastard! You two disgust me!

361
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:29,903
Don't you realize that
this woman will send us to jail?

362
00:25:29,986 --> 00:25:32,072
And this woman will destroy us all!

363
00:25:32,239 --> 00:25:33,573
Do you realize that?!

364
00:25:33,657 --> 00:25:36,451
Yes, I know.
We'll all rot together in hell.

365
00:25:36,660 --> 00:25:38,828
Well, I'm glad you got
yourself a one-way ticket.

366
00:25:38,912 --> 00:25:40,330
And you, Camia Cruz…

367
00:25:40,622 --> 00:25:44,042
Listen to me. You'll regret crossing me!

368
00:25:45,043 --> 00:25:47,379
I'll make you regret ever being born!

369
00:25:47,462 --> 00:25:49,714
-Let's go. Let's go.
-You worthless bastards!

370
00:25:53,093 --> 00:25:54,261
[Emilia] Let's go!

371
00:26:00,767 --> 00:26:01,768
Let's go, Dad.

372
00:26:12,737 --> 00:26:14,864
[Julio] Damn! Damn!

373
00:26:16,241 --> 00:26:17,450
Damn that woman.

374
00:26:20,328 --> 00:26:23,123
Papa, let's stop this.

375
00:26:23,206 --> 00:26:25,375
We shouldn't be the ones fighting.

376
00:26:25,458 --> 00:26:28,169
We have to be united against Camia.

377
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:31,965
You're right. I agree.

378
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:34,467
But on one condition.

379
00:26:34,634 --> 00:26:37,846
Okay, Papa. Tell me anything. I'll do it.

380
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:40,640
Get rid of Raul!

381
00:26:40,974 --> 00:26:43,476
I'm telling you. He's a threat!

382
00:26:44,561 --> 00:26:46,646
He might just betray us.

383
00:26:47,272 --> 00:26:50,066
I understand, Papa. I'll take care of him.

384
00:26:51,484 --> 00:26:54,946
Finally! My daughter is back!

385
00:27:01,119 --> 00:27:03,830
-This is all my fault.
-Yes, Dad. It is.

386
00:27:05,081 --> 00:27:07,667
Mrs. Camia was right.
What you did was unforgivable.

387
00:27:10,754 --> 00:27:13,256
Do you hate me now too, Diego?

388
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:17,761
I don't know, Dad.

389
00:27:19,679 --> 00:27:23,224
But one thing's for sure.
I don't trust you anymore.

390
00:27:24,559 --> 00:27:25,560
I understand.

391
00:27:28,396 --> 00:27:29,731
I promise you this…

392
00:27:32,275 --> 00:27:33,443
I'll change for the better.

393
00:27:35,403 --> 00:27:37,030
I'll earn back your trust in me.

394
00:27:39,115 --> 00:27:40,116
I hope so, Dad.

395
00:27:42,452 --> 00:27:43,536
But don't just promise.

396
00:27:44,537 --> 00:27:45,497
Do it.

397
00:27:47,374 --> 00:27:49,084
I hope you mean what you say.

398
00:27:53,004 --> 00:27:56,049
What's wrong with you, Arnaldo?

399
00:27:57,008 --> 00:28:00,136
I noticed you've been deep in thought.

400
00:28:01,429 --> 00:28:02,889
For some time now.

401
00:28:07,394 --> 00:28:09,646
I'm just trying to figure out
your next move, Grandpa.

402
00:28:09,854 --> 00:28:13,233
I was wondering if I'd make the same move

403
00:28:13,316 --> 00:28:15,985
if I were in your situation.

404
00:28:17,070 --> 00:28:18,071
[laughs]

405
00:28:18,780 --> 00:28:19,864
You know what?

406
00:28:20,573 --> 00:28:25,412
There's no such thing
as the absolute right move.

407
00:28:26,329 --> 00:28:27,497
What matters is…

408
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:31,292
you cling to the absolute truth

409
00:28:31,376 --> 00:28:33,420
when it comes to the Ardiente family,

410
00:28:34,003 --> 00:28:35,171
which is…

411
00:28:36,089 --> 00:28:40,593
nobody can ever bring us down.

412
00:28:41,678 --> 00:28:43,638
As for Camia Cruz? [scoffs]

413
00:28:44,806 --> 00:28:48,685
She's nothing without those
witnesses she's been hiding.

414
00:28:49,394 --> 00:28:51,688
And I know you're trying
your best to find them.

415
00:28:52,605 --> 00:28:53,606
Definitely.

416
00:28:55,191 --> 00:28:58,027
I swear I'll find where they're hiding.

417
00:28:58,778 --> 00:28:59,904
And I believe you.

418
00:29:00,905 --> 00:29:04,159
And now, we can have a good night's sleep.

419
00:29:05,034 --> 00:29:08,246
Just think of Camia…

420
00:29:08,329 --> 00:29:10,373
as a nightmare.

421
00:29:10,832 --> 00:29:12,876
You're doing very well, Arnaldo.

422
00:29:13,376 --> 00:29:14,461
Take your rest.

423
00:29:14,669 --> 00:29:16,004
Okay. Good night.

424
00:29:16,504 --> 00:29:17,589
Good night.

425
00:29:21,259 --> 00:29:24,179
<i>All those who oppose me…</i>

426
00:29:24,679 --> 00:29:26,306
<i>will be silenced.</i>

427
00:29:26,723 --> 00:29:28,933
<i>Especially you, Camia Cruz.</i>

428
00:29:29,434 --> 00:29:33,313
<i>No one can bring the Ardientes down…</i>

429
00:29:33,855 --> 00:29:35,815
<i>as long as I'm alive.</i>

430
00:30:07,764 --> 00:30:11,768
[instrumental theme music playing]

431
00:30:39,504 --> 00:30:43,091
[Ivy] Mom, you'll be staying here for now.

432
00:30:43,716 --> 00:30:46,636
But Lily, why can't I stay
in your rest house?

433
00:30:46,719 --> 00:30:48,263
You can't.

434
00:30:49,597 --> 00:30:52,100
The rest house is under my name.

435
00:30:52,183 --> 00:30:54,310
It's too dangerous for you to stay there.

436
00:30:54,519 --> 00:30:55,562
But…

437
00:30:55,645 --> 00:30:57,689
Can you sleep here tonight?

438
00:30:59,566 --> 00:31:01,442
Mom, I want to, but…

439
00:31:02,318 --> 00:31:05,655
I need to go home to my
house here in Ardiente.

440
00:31:05,738 --> 00:31:09,492
I don't want our enemies
getting suspicious.

441
00:31:11,119 --> 00:31:12,662
I understand.

442
00:31:13,496 --> 00:31:14,706
But be careful over there.

443
00:31:15,081 --> 00:31:16,916
I will, Mom. You too.

444
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:19,210
Your bodyguards will stay with you.

445
00:31:20,003 --> 00:31:21,504
And I'll always check on you.

446
00:31:25,300 --> 00:31:27,385
-Goodnight, Mom. I love you.
-I love you. Good night.

447
00:31:27,468 --> 00:31:28,970
Let's just call each other.

448
00:31:29,470 --> 00:31:30,930
[Ivy] All right. You should get some rest.

449
00:31:54,162 --> 00:31:57,707
Raul, I'm giving you one last chance.

450
00:31:58,041 --> 00:32:01,544
If you pull that stunt again,
I will kill you myself.

451
00:32:02,420 --> 00:32:05,340
I'd much rather see you dead
than see you end up with Camia.

452
00:32:06,507 --> 00:32:07,967
I don't care.

453
00:32:09,552 --> 00:32:10,970
Oh, really now?

454
00:32:11,763 --> 00:32:14,515
What if I have her killed again?

455
00:32:15,683 --> 00:32:18,853
Just so you know,
Papa told me to get rid of you.

456
00:32:19,270 --> 00:32:22,523
But because I love you,
I'm giving you one last chance.

457
00:32:22,815 --> 00:32:24,734
So don't try to betray me.

458
00:32:28,613 --> 00:32:29,614
Understand?

459
00:32:38,665 --> 00:32:42,669
They're going to arraign
our case against the Ardientes.

460
00:32:43,044 --> 00:32:45,296
And they'll definitely plead not guilty.

461
00:32:45,380 --> 00:32:47,507
We need to be ready for the trial.

462
00:32:47,757 --> 00:32:49,759
We will study everyone's testimony

463
00:32:49,842 --> 00:32:52,720
to make sure nobody makes any mistakes.

464
00:32:53,054 --> 00:32:56,432
What will happen to us
after the case, Attorney?

465
00:32:56,516 --> 00:32:58,476
Yeah. And what happens if we lose?

466
00:32:59,310 --> 00:33:00,645
Will they still protect us?

467
00:33:01,521 --> 00:33:04,857
Of course. I will protect you.

468
00:33:05,775 --> 00:33:08,528
And the Ardientes won't defeat us…

469
00:33:08,987 --> 00:33:13,491
because the truth is on our side. Right?

470
00:33:13,783 --> 00:33:16,828
-But they can still twist it.
-If you let them.

471
00:33:19,038 --> 00:33:21,374
If you let yourselves become cowards.

472
00:33:22,291 --> 00:33:23,292
Remember this…

473
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:27,130
we are all victims of the Ardientes.

474
00:33:28,965 --> 00:33:30,758
They used all of you…

475
00:33:31,634 --> 00:33:33,386
to carry out their evil plans.

476
00:33:33,970 --> 00:33:38,766
Now, it's time to right your wrongs.

477
00:33:39,058 --> 00:33:41,561
She's right. We need to trust her.

478
00:33:42,145 --> 00:33:44,522
She'll protect us and our families.

479
00:33:46,190 --> 00:33:48,651
Justice will finally be served
for my sister's death…

480
00:33:49,318 --> 00:33:51,112
and the murders
of all those innocent people.

481
00:33:52,113 --> 00:33:54,657
The Ardientes will
finally be brought down.

482
00:33:56,409 --> 00:33:57,702
Which is why…

483
00:34:00,288 --> 00:34:01,706
we will all work together

484
00:34:01,789 --> 00:34:04,667
to bring down the Ardientes.

485
00:34:06,502 --> 00:34:07,795
Understood?

486
00:34:12,133 --> 00:34:14,886
Attorney, it's not safe here.

487
00:34:15,803 --> 00:34:18,014
We need to move them all
to the safe house.

488
00:34:30,818 --> 00:34:31,736
[knocking on door]

489
00:34:31,819 --> 00:34:34,906
[secretary] Mayor, these are
from the social welfare office.

490
00:34:34,989 --> 00:34:37,033
These are the documents you asked for.

491
00:34:38,201 --> 00:34:39,327
Just leave them there.

492
00:34:39,410 --> 00:34:41,204
And take these signed documents.

493
00:34:42,246 --> 00:34:43,456
Thank you, sir.

494
00:34:43,539 --> 00:34:47,668
Um, Mayor, what are those
files from DSWD for?

495
00:34:48,419 --> 00:34:51,255
Why are you asking
so many questions? Get out.

496
00:34:51,339 --> 00:34:53,591
I'm sorry. I'm just concerned about you,

497
00:34:53,674 --> 00:34:55,176
especially after what I watched on TV.

498
00:34:55,259 --> 00:34:58,387
I don't want you to lose your position
because I might lose my job too.

499
00:34:58,471 --> 00:35:01,307
You'll lose your job if you
don't get out of my sight.

500
00:35:01,390 --> 00:35:02,517
I'm sorry.

501
00:35:07,730 --> 00:35:11,359
[sinister music playing]

502
00:35:33,089 --> 00:35:35,508
I'm okay, Mom. I just went home…

503
00:35:35,591 --> 00:35:38,970
to get a few things.
I'll leave here right away.

504
00:35:39,053 --> 00:35:40,221
[Edward] <i>Be careful, Maria.</i>

505
00:35:40,304 --> 00:35:43,474
Text us as soon as you get
back to your aunt's house.

506
00:35:43,933 --> 00:35:46,477
And don't go out, okay?

507
00:35:46,561 --> 00:35:49,564
They already sent some men
over to keep you safe.

508
00:35:49,730 --> 00:35:50,773
Okay, Mom.

509
00:35:52,191 --> 00:35:53,192
Okay.

510
00:35:53,526 --> 00:35:56,571
Esther, Edward… Are you okay?

511
00:35:56,654 --> 00:35:58,030
Is there a problem?

512
00:35:58,865 --> 00:36:01,659
No. We just checked on our daughter.

513
00:36:02,034 --> 00:36:03,369
-That's right.
-She seems fine.

514
00:36:03,911 --> 00:36:05,913
She just dropped by our house
to get some things.

515
00:36:06,372 --> 00:36:08,583
But she said she'll go back
to her aunt straight away.

516
00:36:09,083 --> 00:36:10,459
That's good to hear.

517
00:36:11,085 --> 00:36:13,045
You need to go. They're waiting for you.

518
00:36:13,129 --> 00:36:15,464
Okay. Let's go, Edward.

519
00:36:21,762 --> 00:36:24,015
[ominous music playing]

520
00:36:42,033 --> 00:36:43,159
-[muffled screams]
-[man grunts]

521
00:36:44,410 --> 00:36:47,205
[muffled screams]

522
00:36:55,588 --> 00:36:57,048
Okay. Bring her inside.

523
00:36:57,423 --> 00:36:58,799
[goon] Hurry. Get in.

524
00:37:12,104 --> 00:37:13,231
Here you go, dear.

525
00:37:13,606 --> 00:37:15,316
I missed cooking for you.

526
00:37:15,650 --> 00:37:16,734
It's your favorite!

527
00:37:17,610 --> 00:37:18,694
Thank you, Mom.

528
00:37:22,657 --> 00:37:23,658
Lily.

529
00:37:24,367 --> 00:37:26,827
Is there something bothering you?

530
00:37:31,707 --> 00:37:33,668
I'm just thinking about…

531
00:37:34,794 --> 00:37:36,337
our witnesses.

532
00:37:37,046 --> 00:37:40,675
They've sacrificed a lot
for their families too.

533
00:37:43,594 --> 00:37:44,845
That's why…

534
00:37:46,264 --> 00:37:49,850
I'm more determined
to bring the Ardientes down.

535
00:37:50,184 --> 00:37:51,227
Especially now that…

536
00:37:51,936 --> 00:37:54,313
we have everything we
need to present in court.

537
00:37:55,189 --> 00:37:59,193
The Ardientes won't stand a chance.

538
00:38:08,577 --> 00:38:11,163
[Julio] Make sure that
everyone who's important…

539
00:38:11,247 --> 00:38:12,748
will be there tonight.

540
00:38:13,040 --> 00:38:15,501
-Yes, Congressman.
-That'll be all. You can go.

541
00:38:21,841 --> 00:38:23,009
Hey, Arnaldo.

542
00:38:28,639 --> 00:38:29,515
[Julio chuckles]

543
00:38:29,932 --> 00:38:32,435
What's with that smile on your face?

544
00:38:32,643 --> 00:38:36,188
Does this mean that you've found
what you were looking for?

545
00:38:38,024 --> 00:38:40,776
Yes. I know where they are.

546
00:38:41,652 --> 00:38:43,404
Make sure that…

547
00:38:43,487 --> 00:38:46,032
each and every one of those witnesses…

548
00:38:47,033 --> 00:38:51,287
regrets their decision to
go up against the Ardientes.

549
00:38:53,414 --> 00:38:56,709
I want each of them to suffer.

550
00:39:05,885 --> 00:39:09,096
[phone ringing]

551
00:39:11,849 --> 00:39:15,353
[phone ringing]

552
00:39:18,105 --> 00:39:22,109
[phone ringing]

553
00:39:26,864 --> 00:39:30,534
[phone ringing]

554
00:39:31,827 --> 00:39:35,664
[phone ringing]

555
00:39:39,710 --> 00:39:40,920
-Hello, Dad?
-Hello…

556
00:39:41,003 --> 00:39:42,630
Diego. I'm glad you picked up.

557
00:39:43,089 --> 00:39:44,090
What is it?

558
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:47,676
Do you know how to get
in touch with Camia?

559
00:39:49,011 --> 00:39:50,846
Dad, can you please stop it?

560
00:39:50,930 --> 00:39:52,556
<i>Listen to me, Diego.</i>

561
00:39:53,474 --> 00:39:55,851
Your grandfather already
knows where Camia's hiding

562
00:39:55,935 --> 00:39:58,145
the witnesses against the Ardientes.

563
00:39:58,896 --> 00:40:00,147
<i>You should tell Camia.</i>

564
00:40:01,023 --> 00:40:02,900
Okay, Dad. Leave it to me.

565
00:40:11,534 --> 00:40:15,287
[Emilia] Ivy, I'm so glad that
you're back in Ardiente.

566
00:40:15,371 --> 00:40:18,124
I finally have someone
to confide my problems to.

567
00:40:18,624 --> 00:40:22,336
Not just yet. Because, I
won't be staying here long.

568
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:24,130
-Sit down, Emilia.
-Thank you.

569
00:40:24,713 --> 00:40:28,509
I need to oversee my
other businesses in Manila.

570
00:40:29,260 --> 00:40:30,553
Besides…

571
00:40:30,636 --> 00:40:32,513
Congressman and I
aren't on good terms yet.

572
00:40:32,596 --> 00:40:35,558
So, I'm a little worried that…

573
00:40:36,183 --> 00:40:38,686
he might have me killed.

574
00:40:39,645 --> 00:40:42,314
Hey, I'd like to apologize
about the press conference.

575
00:40:42,648 --> 00:40:44,817
I hope it doesn't ruin our relationship.

576
00:40:45,526 --> 00:40:46,986
You know, that fiasco thing?

577
00:40:48,446 --> 00:40:51,740
Well, I understand. I need to understand.

578
00:40:54,034 --> 00:40:56,579
You're facing a huge problem, Emilia.

579
00:40:56,662 --> 00:40:58,831
I bet it's giving you a headache.

580
00:40:58,914 --> 00:40:59,957
[sighs]

581
00:41:00,040 --> 00:41:03,294
Well, the only person giving us
a headache is that Camia.

582
00:41:03,711 --> 00:41:04,712
But, you know…

583
00:41:04,795 --> 00:41:08,215
I believe that all headaches can be cured.

584
00:41:09,425 --> 00:41:10,426
Really?

585
00:41:10,885 --> 00:41:14,180
Are you sure that Camia
is just a headache?

586
00:41:15,598 --> 00:41:19,602
Isn't Camia Cruz somewhat…

587
00:41:19,685 --> 00:41:21,020
like a cancer,

588
00:41:21,437 --> 00:41:23,105
who is out to kill the Ardientes?

589
00:41:23,189 --> 00:41:24,190
[Emilia scoffs]

590
00:41:24,648 --> 00:41:28,819
Ivy, there's a solution
to every problem, right?

591
00:41:29,236 --> 00:41:31,655
Especially now that Papa
and I have patched things up.

592
00:41:34,617 --> 00:41:36,243
You've patched things up with your father?

593
00:41:36,327 --> 00:41:38,662
-Yes, Ivy.
-I'm happy for you.

594
00:41:38,746 --> 00:41:40,080
At… At least.

595
00:41:40,164 --> 00:41:43,959
I know. That's why
I've decided to postpone

596
00:41:44,043 --> 00:41:46,170
all my plans against him.

597
00:41:46,253 --> 00:41:48,881
What's important now is that we're united…

598
00:41:48,964 --> 00:41:50,508
in our battle against Camia.

599
00:41:51,967 --> 00:41:54,553
Hey, I hate to do this.
But I have to go, Ivy.

600
00:41:54,637 --> 00:41:56,263
You know that I'm very busy.

601
00:41:56,972 --> 00:41:58,349
Thank you for your time.

602
00:41:58,432 --> 00:42:00,601
[chuckles] Leaving so soon?

603
00:42:00,684 --> 00:42:02,561
What are you so busy with?

604
00:42:02,645 --> 00:42:04,772
We didn't even have time

605
00:42:04,855 --> 00:42:07,608
to drink wine or--

606
00:42:07,691 --> 00:42:10,861
Well, next time, Ivy.
Thank you again for your time.

607
00:42:11,654 --> 00:42:14,740
I really hope you win
the case against Camia.

608
00:42:14,823 --> 00:42:17,493
It would make me so sad to see you…

609
00:42:17,993 --> 00:42:19,537
go to jail, Emilia.

610
00:42:20,079 --> 00:42:21,455
Thank you for your concern, Ivy.

611
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:23,791
I have to go. Bye.

612
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:27,962
Hey! What's he doing here?

613
00:42:29,255 --> 00:42:30,297
[Ivy] Oh.

614
00:42:31,257 --> 00:42:34,260
Diego called me earlier to tell me

615
00:42:34,343 --> 00:42:37,930
that there's something we need
to discuss about the farmers.

616
00:42:38,013 --> 00:42:39,890
Something to consult me about.

617
00:42:40,683 --> 00:42:42,893
Well, I told him that it wouldn't hurt

618
00:42:42,977 --> 00:42:44,728
if I listen to him. Right?

619
00:42:46,230 --> 00:42:48,274
Okay. I'll get going. Bye again.

620
00:42:48,816 --> 00:42:49,942
-Bye, Emilia.
-Bye.

621
00:42:58,909 --> 00:43:00,995
Diego, what are you doing here?

622
00:43:02,746 --> 00:43:03,789
Ivy…

623
00:43:03,872 --> 00:43:07,293
The Ardientes already know where
you're hiding the witnesses.

624
00:43:15,759 --> 00:43:17,011
[Julio] Don't worry.

625
00:43:17,678 --> 00:43:20,055
This issue will all be over soon.

626
00:43:20,681 --> 00:43:23,684
Right now, our lawyers are looking into

627
00:43:23,767 --> 00:43:26,562
how they can shut that Camia Cruz up.

628
00:43:26,645 --> 00:43:29,940
But, in the meantime,
let's just work for the people.

629
00:43:30,024 --> 00:43:34,111
Congressman, our friends
from the press are inviting you

630
00:43:34,194 --> 00:43:36,196
for an exclusive interview.

631
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:37,615
Will you accept the invite?

632
00:43:37,698 --> 00:43:39,283
Why not?

633
00:43:39,783 --> 00:43:41,744
I'll tell my staff to call them up

634
00:43:41,827 --> 00:43:44,330
so we can schedule an interview
as soon as possible.

635
00:43:44,413 --> 00:43:45,414
[chuckles]

636
00:43:45,956 --> 00:43:48,208
I admire your confidence, Congressman.

637
00:43:48,292 --> 00:43:51,670
This issue will be put to rest
sooner than expected.

638
00:43:51,754 --> 00:43:53,088
You bet, Governor.

639
00:43:54,673 --> 00:43:55,758
To the congressman.

640
00:43:56,675 --> 00:43:58,469
-To the congressman.
-Okay!

641
00:44:01,221 --> 00:44:03,891
Are you sure, Diego? How is that possible?

642
00:44:03,974 --> 00:44:07,186
And where did you get that information?

643
00:44:07,269 --> 00:44:08,604
My dad told me.

644
00:44:09,188 --> 00:44:10,189
[scoffs]

645
00:44:11,482 --> 00:44:13,317
Your father told you?

646
00:44:14,610 --> 00:44:17,988
Well, I don't trust your father.
You know that, right, Diego?

647
00:44:18,822 --> 00:44:21,158
And if you'll keep believing him…

648
00:44:21,950 --> 00:44:23,535
Diego, I'm sorry,

649
00:44:23,619 --> 00:44:26,830
but maybe I shouldn't trust you either.

650
00:44:28,582 --> 00:44:29,833
I understand how you feel, Ivy.

651
00:44:30,417 --> 00:44:32,753
But it wouldn't hurt to take precautions.

652
00:44:32,836 --> 00:44:35,798
[dramatic music playing]

653
00:44:46,433 --> 00:44:47,476
<i>Mayor,</i>

654
00:44:47,935 --> 00:44:51,105
<i>have you found a way</i>
<i>to silence that woman?</i>

655
00:44:51,188 --> 00:44:52,272
<i>What's it to you?</i>

656
00:44:52,356 --> 00:44:54,400
<i>Your assignment is</i>
<i>to look after my mother.</i>

657
00:44:54,942 --> 00:44:58,278
[Raul] <i>I can help Camia more if</i>
<i>I stay here with the Ardientes.</i>

658
00:44:58,362 --> 00:44:59,405
<i>You traitor!</i>

659
00:44:59,488 --> 00:45:01,448
<i>I will find out who you're working with!</i>

660
00:45:03,826 --> 00:45:05,452
[Arnaldo] <i>Answer me when I'm asking you!</i>

661
00:45:05,536 --> 00:45:07,037
<i>Where is your safe house? </i>[cocks gun]

662
00:45:07,121 --> 00:45:08,288
<i>-Sir, don't! No!</i>
<i>-No, Sir! No!</i>

663
00:45:08,372 --> 00:45:09,289
<i>Esther and Edward…</i>

664
00:45:09,373 --> 00:45:10,374
<i>-are in danger.</i>
-[gunshots]

665
00:45:10,457 --> 00:45:13,961
[Ivy] <i>All our witnesses need to transfer</i>
<i>to another safe house.</i>

666
00:45:14,044 --> 00:45:15,504
<i>I need to go there now.</i>

667
00:45:15,587 --> 00:45:19,007
[theme music playing]
